From 096b04c159339f58061e381b418924c8de9bb7c4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: halt95 <halt95@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 09:50:32 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 88/97] kv: side-cache layout -- fold the PLE state into a GDN
 group, pack QSA rings

The packed pool strides every block by the widest group, and every group draws whole blocks. The PLE short-conv
state now shares a GDN cache group, and the QSA raw-key rings are packed as equal slots inside shared blocks, so
neither holds a whole block per request. VLLM_E2_SIDE_CACHE_LAYOUT (default 1) selects the old layout with 0.
On its own the layout raises the Flash-Next pool from 806,792 to 853,994 tokens at the same budget.
